    "title": "How to watch the 2026 World Baseball Classic: Full schedule, where to stream games free and more",
    "text": "Team USA has made it to the quarterfinals of the 2026 World Baseball Classic, here's how to watch all the remaining games of the tournament. (Rob Tringali/WBCI/MLB Photos via Getty Images) (Rob Tringali via Getty Images)The World Baseball Classic is an international baseball tournament that first began in 2006 as an event sanctioned by the World Baseball Softball Confederation, and it's the only international baseball championship of national teams that features the participation of professional players. (You can see a complete list of MLB players participating here.) The latest installment of the World Baseball Classic has just wrapped up pool play and the quarterfinals will take place this Friday and Saturday, with notable matchups between Team USA and Canada, and reigning champion Japan facing Venezuela. The championship final will take place in Miami on March 17, 2026.Remaining WBC games will be split between FOX, FS1, FS2, and FOX Deportes, and all of them will stream on FOX One. Here's everything you need to know about how to watch the 2026 World Baseball Classic including a complete schedule of games and where to watch them all.AdvertisementDates: March 4-17, 2026Channels: FOX, FS1, FS2, and FOX DeportesStreaming: FOX One, DirecTV, Fubo, Tubi & moreWhat channels will air the 2026 World Baseball Classic?Almost all of this year's World Baseball Classic games will air on either FOX, FS1, or FS2, and 41 of the 47 games in the tournament will also be broadcast in Spanish on FOX Deportes. A select few games will be available on the Fox Sports App and/or Tubi. The Championship Game in Miami on Tuesday, March 17 will air on Fox.Where to watch the World Baseball Classic without cableEvery single World Baseball Classic game will stream on FOX One. You can also catch games that are broadcast on Fox, FS1 and FS2 on platforms like DirecTV and Fubo.FOX One is a new streaming service from FOX that launched in 2025. With a subscription to FOX One, you can tune in to all your favorite FOX channels like FOX News, FOX Sports, FOX Weather, FS1, FS2, FOX Business, FOX Deportes, Big Ten Network (B1G), and local FOX stations all in one place, and this year, they'll be streaming every single game of the 2026 World Baseball Classic. FOX One offers live programming, as well as shows and movies on demand. The base price for FOX One will cost $19.99 a month, or you can save with an annual subscription for $199.99. World Baseball Classic PoolsPool A: Canada, Colombia, Cuba, Panama and Puerto RicoAdvertisementPool B: Brazil, Great Britain, Italy, Mexico and United StatesPool C: Australia, Chinese Taipei, Czechia, Japan and KoreaPool D: Dominican Republic, Israel, Netherlands, Nicaragua and VenezuelaWorld Baseball Classic ScheduleSunday, March 15, 2026United States @ Dominican Republic: 8:00 PM ET (FOX, FS1)Monday, March 16, 2026Venezuela @ Italy: 8:00 PM ET (FS1)Tuesday, March 17, 2026TBD @ TBD: 8:00 PM ET (FOX)",
